1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--phrase-memorization","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/phrase-memorization","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/phrase-memorization","sourceHash":"ad770547594d997aec3c9314e2c9d00a9559dad070b30436c993af14e718f78f","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:10:57.512Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Phrase Memorization","zh":"短语记忆"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Phrase memorization means learning ready-to-use chunks of language — complete phrases and expressions that you can deploy in conversation without having to construct them from scratch.","zh":"短语记忆是指学习可以直接使用的语言组块——无需从头组织、可直接用于对话的完整短语和表达。"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"A related activity is <a href=\"/roadmap/library/mad-libs-learning\">Mad-libs Learning</a>","zh":"一种相关的活动是<a href=\"/roadmap/library/mad-libs-learning\">填空式学习</a>"}},{"id":"why-it-helps","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why It Helps","zh":"为什么有帮助"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"When you're under the pressure of real-time conversation, your brain doesn't have time to assemble every sentence from individual words and grammar rules. Having a bank of pre-memorized phrases gives you reliable fallbacks: greetings, common questions, polite requests, reactions, and situation-specific expressions.","zh":"在实时对话的压力下，大脑没有时间用单个词汇和语法规则逐句拼装表达。储备一批预先记忆的短语，能为你提供可靠的备用表达，例如问候、常见问题、礼貌请求、回应以及特定情境中的用语。"}},{"id":"examples","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Examples","zh":"示例"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"\"Could you repeat that, please?\"","zh":"“请再说一遍，可以吗？”"},{"en":"\"What does the word ___ mean?\"","zh":"“___ 这个词是什么意思？”"},{"en":"\"I'd like to order this, please\"","zh":"“我想点这个，谢谢。”"},{"en":"\"Excuse me, where is bathroom?\"","zh":"“不好意思，请问洗手间在哪里？”"},{"en":"Common greetings and farewells for your target dialect","zh":"目标方言中常用的问候语和告别语"}]},{"id":"how-to-learn-them","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How to Learn Them","zh":"如何学习这些短语"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Create flashcards with the phrase and its meaning/context","zh":"制作包含短语及其含义或使用语境的闪卡"},{"en":"Audio for many phrases can be found through <a href=\"https://youglish.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">YouGlish</a>","zh":"许多短语的音频都可以通过<a href=\"https://youglish.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">YouGlish</a>找到"},{"en":"Practice saying them out loud until they feel natural <a href=\"/roadmap/library/chorusing\">Chorusing</a>","zh":"反复大声练习，直到说起来感觉自然<a href=\"/roadmap/library/chorusing\">齐声跟读法</a>"},{"en":"Use them in real conversations as soon as possible — the real-world reinforcement is what makes them stick","zh":"尽快在真实对话中使用这些短语——现实中的强化练习才能让它们真正牢记于心"}]},{"id":"when-its-relevant","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When It's Relevant","zh":"何时适用"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Phrase memorization is most useful in Phase 4X (Situational Speaking), where you're preparing for specific real-life situations. It's also valuable any time you're about to enter a new domain where you need functional language quickly (travel, a new job, etc.).","zh":"短语记忆在阶段 4X（情境口语）中最为实用，因为此时你正在为特定的现实生活情境做准备。每当你即将进入一个需要迅速掌握实用语言的新领域时，它也很有价值，例如旅行或开始一份新工作。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
